14.1%. Not 15.67%. Hmm, 0.15666*24 = 3.76 days. If \"today\" boundaries use noon? Hmm.\n\nMaybe progress = 1 - (remaining days - fraction?) no. Let's compute if progress fraction uses hours: 3.76 days elapsed means 14 Nov 18:15. It's 9:04 device time. Unless timezone difference of ~9 hours? The app might compute with UTC (device time is UTC+9? Tokyo?). If device time is 9:04 JST and period started Nov 11 00:00 local, elapsed = 3.38 days. If app uses UTC, Nov 14 00:04 UTC = 3.0 days = 12.5%. Hmm 3.76?\n\nMaybe progress = elapsed/total where total 24 days and elapsed 3.76: Actually if the period started Nov 11 and \"ends\" Dec 4 (inclusive), elapsed = 3 days + time-of-day = 3.38. Hmm.\n\nWhat if progress bar represents \"budget used over time\"? Hmm 0.1566... =? 66/100=0.66; 34/100=0.34; 40/100=0.4; 60/100=0.6. None.\n\nCould be days remaining fraction: 20 remaining /24 = 0.833; 1-0.833=0.167. Close to 0.1567 but not equal.\n\nProgress = (24 - 20.24)/24? Hmm.\n\nLet me compute precisely: 0.15666668 * 24 = 3.76000032 days. 3.76 days = 3 days 18h14m. At 09:04 local, that'd be 14:46 if UTC+... hmm not.\n\nMaybe total period days is 23.44? Ugh.\n\nAlternatively progress = 1 - daysRemaining/totalDays where daysRemaining is fractional 20.24: 1 - 20.24/24 = 0.1567! Yes! If days remaining = 20.24 (i.e., 20 days 5.8 hours), then 1-0.8433=0.1567. And elapsed = 3.76. Hmm, days remaining 20.24 would be from Nov 14 09:04 to Dec 4 15:00? Weird.\n\nHmm, if remaining days = 20.24 = 20 days + 5.76h, then end = Nov 14 09:04 + 20.24d = Dec 4 14:49. Not midnight.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the day boundary is at midnight and the current time 09:04 gives remaining from Nov 14 09:04 to Dec 4 00:00 = 19 days 14.9h = 19.62 days. 20 - 19.62? Hmm. Total period Nov 11 00:00 → Dec 4 00:00 = 23 days, not 24. But UI says 24 days (inclusive).\n\nTime progress = elapsed/total where elapsed from Nov 11 00:00 to Nov 14 09:04 = 3.378d; /24 = 0.1408. Not 0.1567.\n\nIf end is Dec 4 23:59:59 (24 days from Nov 11 00:00 to Dec 5 00:00), elapsed/total = 3.378/24 = 0.1407. Hmm.\n\n0.1567*24 = 3.76. Suspicious: exactly 3.76 could be 3 days + 18.24h; maybe device timezone vs app timezone.\n\nHmm, maybe the period started at 11 Nov 15:00? because budget created at ? The preconditions said current period started 3 days ago. Maybe it was created at 15:00 on Nov 11 (local) — elapsed to Nov 14 09:04 = 2.75 days. no.\n\nI can't prove progress-bar wrong. Skip.\n\nNow — bigger question: are there any obvious functional bugs I've found so far? Let me list candidates:\n1. Negative expense (1-5 = -$4) — saved as +$4 refund increasing total budget 100→104; banner preview said \"Daily Amount exceeded / For tomorrow $1.8\" (inconsistent with refund). Also after saving, history shows Today Total: $0 (not -$4 or +$4?) — inconsistent: entry displays +$4 but today's total $0. That's a real internal inconsistency! Let's examine: History row showed \"Transport +$4\" and \"Total: $0\". If the section total is sum of displayed amounts, it should be +$4 (or at least nonzero). And the header Total budget changed to $104 while \"Total: $0\" today. Hmm. The \"Total\" might count only expenses (positive) and exclude refunds: sum of positive = 0 → Total $0. But then the displayed refund isn't counted anywhere except budget increase. It's confusing but could be by design (refunds aren't part of spent total).\n\nHmm, wait. Actually maybe the negative amount entry was NOT saved as refund but as something that increased budget. The row's green +$4 suggests refund. Today Total $0 excludes refunds. The budget sheet spent stayed 60. So the refund added to the budget (100→104). This is likely \"income\" semantics: negative expense = income, added to budget total. Hmm, but then the history total excluding income makes sense, and the banner \"For tomorrow\" should account for income. The preview banner used the wrong sign though.\n\nIs that a real bug worth reporting? The visible inconsistency: With amount -$4 pending, the daily warning says \"Daily Amount exceeded. For tomorrow $1.8\" even though saving increases available budget. After saving, available becomes 44 (42%). And \"Daily Amount exceeded\" was false. I think it's a legitimate bug report (wrong value/computation for negative amounts), though a bit speculative. Maybe better to reproduce once with cleaner baseline and capture exact texts. I'll do that later.\n\n2. Very large amounts allowed (99999999999999999999+1 = $100000000000000000000) — saving such would probably be prevented? We didn't save. Not a bug necessarily.\n\n3. Historical per-date sections: not yet tested for lazy building.\n\n4. Category management: icons not visible in grid cards; need more investigation.\n\n5. Back button exits app from modal/sheet (dismiss behavior). Minor.\n\nLet me look for the category management screen more. Hmm, maybe it's reachable by tapping the selected category chip when in NON-list mode? We long-pressed and saw Delete Category. Maybe tapping the \"Category\" chip (tag) when non-list mode opens inline create; and long-press a category chip gives Delete. That's all the management there is. But the changed feature says \"Category management screen\". Maybe the grid in list mode IS the management screen? The cards show category names only with no icons, despite the feature \"category icons are now resolved together with the category list\". This is likely where the injected bug lives: category icons not showing on the cards. \n\nHow can I verify that icons SHOULD show? The card has a large empty area above the label — strongly suggests an icon slot. The card height ~342px with label at bottom-left; empty top area. Compare: the \"Category limits\" list rows had icons? No, those rows also had no icons (Transport/Food rows with \"No limit\"), but they had no empty icon slot (text starts at left). \n\nIn the grid cards, the label is at the bottom-left and the top half is blank. That's a big blank area — likely the category icon. If icons were resolved, we'd see e.g., a bus for Transport, a fork for Food, a coffee cup for Coffee. Since all are blank, icons are missing. Hmm, but maybe the cards just have a large padding and label at bottom by design (no icon feature). The changed line says \"category icons are now resolved together with th", "truncated": true}
