ed chip's tag icon is wrong — the actual icon should be e.g. Food's icon. The developer might consider chips show icons.\n\nHmm.\n\nLet me test the chip icons in non-list mode by selecting each category and seeing the icon:\n- We saw selected Food showed tag icon; selected Transport tag; selected Coffee tag. All identical tag icon → clearly not per-category icons. But maybe the generic tag is intended as the \"selected\" indicator.\n\nUgh.\n\nLet me look at the category limits screen again: rows have no icons. If icons were part of category data, the limits screen would likely show them. It doesn't. So maybe categories have no icons at all in this app, and \"category icons\" refers to the emoji/text icon? Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the \"category icons\" are displayed in the *history* list rows, as leading icon? The history rows showed no leading icons. Hmm.\n\nLet me consider the app's actual UI from screenshots: history rows show no icons. Category chips no icons. Category limits no icons. Grid cards no icons. Everything no icons. So maybe the change \"category icons are now resolved together with the category list\" isn't user-visible in these screens, or refers to the tag icon color?\n\nMaybe icons ARE rendered but as a solid single-color shape similar to background? Unlikely.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the category icon is shown only when a category has been assigned an icon via a long-press menu → \"Edit Category\" screen with icon picker? And the long-press menu just showed \"Delete Category\". Maybe the menu has more items if scrolled? Let me long-press a chip again and screenshot the popup to see all options. In non-list mode. Currently list mode is ON (grid mode). Turn it off. Hmm.\n\nActually, earlier long-press Food (non-list) gave elements: \"Food | Delete Category\" and \"Delete Category\" — a dropdown with one item. So only delete.\n\nOK, maybe the management screen is not reachable in this build except via inline add + delete. The icons might be an internal th